  "Id": 979,
  "Title": "Helping victims of oil spill",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "In an effort to minimise the extent of the health hazards caused by the oil spill, Unilever Pakistan with the support of Aga Khan University and Behbud Association took prompt action and set up a medical camp in Shirin Jinnah Colony.",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In an effort to minimise the extent of the health hazards caused by the oil spill, Unilever Pakistan with the support of Aga Khan University and Behbud Association took prompt action and set up a medical camp in Shirin Jinnah Colony. The camp provided free consultation, treatment and medication to health victims of the oil spill by eye, skin, ENT and other specialists. In order to help residents adequately protect themselves from the noxious fumes lingering in the air, free information on precautionary measures was also made available at the camp."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
